<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">7 May in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">7 events that happened on 7 May, from 558 to 1945.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/hagia-sophia" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hagia-sophia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">558 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,468 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Main dome of Hagia Sophia collapses</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Weakened by earthquakes, the great dome of Justinian's cathedral fell. It was rebuilt taller and steeper by Isidore the Younger, and that dome, though repaired, still stands.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hagia-sophia">Hagia Sophia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1664 CE <span class="tih-ago">362 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Louis XIV opens a grand festival at Versailles</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Louis XIV began 'The Pleasures of the Enchanted Island', a week of spectacles and plays including Molière's first Tartuffe. Versailles became the seat of court and government in 1682.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/dutch-empire">Dutch Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/versailles">Versailles</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xiv">Louis XIV</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1718 CE <span class="tih-ago">308 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Bienville founds New Orleans, by tradition on this day</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Jean-Baptiste Le Moyne de Bienville chose a crescent of high ground on the Mississippi for a new French post. The city became a meeting point of French, Spanish, African and American cultures.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1765 CE <span class="tih-ago">261 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">HMS Victory is launched at Chatham</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The 100-gun first-rate HMS Victory was floated out of dry dock at Chatham. Forty years later she was Nelson's flagship at Trafalgar, and she survives at Portsmouth as the oldest commissioned warship.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1824 CE <span class="tih-ago">202 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Beethoven's Ninth Symphony is first performed in Vienna</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Beethoven's Ninth, with its choral setting of Schiller's 'Ode to Joy', premiered at the Kärntnertortheater. The composer, almost entirely deaf, had to be turned to see the audience's applause.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1915 CE <span class="tih-ago">111 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">German U-boat sinks the liner Lusitania</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">U-20 torpedoed the Cunard liner off southern Ireland, sinking her in 18 minutes with the loss of 1,198 lives, 128 of them American. Outrage in the US turned opinion sharply against Germany.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1945 CE <span class="tih-ago">81 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Germany signs its unconditional surrender at Reims</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">General Alfred Jodl signed the surrender at Eisenhower's headquarters, to take effect the next night. A second signing in Berlin followed at Soviet insistence.</p></div></li></ol>
